\n\n**2. Two harness bugs I hit and fixed (not translation bugs).** fd 1 is process-global, so parallel tests stomped each other's redirection, and libtest's own `test NAME ... ok` progress lines leaked into captures. Fixed with a `STDOUT_LOCK` and `.cargo/config.toml` setting `RUST_TEST_THREADS = \"1\"`. Worth knowing: **this suite is only valid single-threaded**, which that config now enforces.\n\nAlso note `cargo` needed `--offline` (the registry fetch is blocked by the proxy); `libloading 0.8.9` was already in the local cache.","ttft_ms":2418,"type":"result","duration_ms":775620,"uuid":"6f7b9dbc-097a-4750-a87e-603191df9ba9","ttft_stream_ms":2288,"time_to_request_ms":54,"first_content_frame_ms":2288,"queued_turn_count":0}
